    "compose_patient": {
      "sections": [
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.0",
          "heading": "why_in_hospital",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came in with a serious infection of the skin and tissue in your left thigh. This is called a necrotising soft-tissue infection. It caused your body to go into shock and affected several organs, including your lungs and kidneys."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "We found two types of bacteria in the wound: Group A Streptococcus and anaerobes.\n\nTo support your body, we:\n- Put a breathing tube in and used a machine to help you breathe.\n- Gave you medicines to support your blood pressure.\n- Used a machine to support your kidneys (CVVH). Your kidneys recovered and this was stopped on day 16.\n- Turned you face-down twice to help your lungs.\n- Fed you through a tube into your stomach until you could eat again.\n\nYour breathing tube was removed on day 18. You moved from intensive care to the ward on day 24.\n\nSurgeons cleaned the wound four times (on days 0, 2, 5, and 9). The wound was then washed out, closed, and a special wound dressing (VAC dressing) was applied. Your wound is still healing. A district nurse and a tissue viability nurse are involved in your wound care.\n\nYou were given strong antibiotics through a drip for a long time. These were changed to the most suitable ones based on the bacteria found.\n\nYou also developed an irregular heartbeat (atrial fibrillation), which was treated to control your heart rate.\n\nYou had a lot of physiotherapy and rehabilitation during your stay."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.7",
            "sections.8"
          ],
          "text": "You have the following appointments and support arranged:\n\n- Plastics and wound clinic at 2 weeks.\n- Cardiology (heart) clinic at 6 weeks for your irregular heartbeat.\n- A follow-up clinic with the intensive care team.\n- Community physiotherapy and occupational therapy.\n\nYour GP will check your kidney function and blood pressure after your kidney injury."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.4",
          "heading": "safety_net",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{SAFETY_NET}}"
        }
